SUMMARY:Gentle Monster
LOCATION:Kendall Square\, 355 Binney St\, Cambridge\, MA 02142
DESCRIPTION:Times: 3:15pm\, 5:50pm\, 6:50pm\nFrom director and writer Marie
  Kreutzer (Corsage\, Austria’s entry for the 95th Academy Awards)\, Gent
 le Monster tells the story of concert pianist Lucy (Léa Seydoux)\, who ha
 s just relocated her family to a country house hoping to ease her husband 
 Philip’s (Laurence Rupp) severe burnout. Before they have a chance to se
 t up their new home\, an early morning police visit tears their life apart
 . Trapped between the man she loves and the fear of what he may have done\
 , Lucy must face the situation alone as her world unravels. With a cast th
 at includes Jella Haase alongside the legendary\, Academy Award nominee Ca
 therine Deneuve\, Gentle Monster asks what we do when someone we love turn
 s out to be someone we never really knew.\nhttps://booking.landmarktheatre
 s.com/launch/ticketing/42ed0323-541d-5e05-852b-50bc2971077f\nFrom Pushpin 
 Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://booking.landmarktheatres.com/launch/ticketing/42ed0323-541d-5e0
 5-852b-50bc2971077f
